<!--
  The STYLED-RECIPE shape, under `output: 'ssr'`.

  Mirrors `packages/ui/registry/card.aihu` / `badge.aihu` / `separator.aihu` /
  `button.aihu` verbatim in structure: a hand-written custom-element class
  declared INSIDE `@state`, with a shared static Constructable StyleSheet and
  an idempotent `customElements.define`.

  This is NOT the `$extends` bug. That one threw at MODULE LOAD, because the
  class sat at the module's own top level and the extends clause is evaluated
  on import. Here the class sits in the component's SETUP BODY, which the
  compiler emits verbatim into `__aihu_setup__` and `__aihu_ssr_string_setup__`
  — so the module imports cleanly and then throws the moment the component is
  actually rendered. Three DOM globals in three lines, any one of which is
  enough: `HTMLElement` (the extends clause), `CSSStyleSheet` (the static field
  initializer), `customElements` (the registration).

  The GUARD below is the fix, and it lives in AUTHORED SOURCE because there is
  nowhere else it can live — no shared function is involved, the compiler emits
  what the author wrote. It is the same condition the compiler puts on its own
  `defineElement` call further down the emitted module. Delete it and this
  element renders empty on every server request (assertion 16); the same shape
  is checked against every shipped recipe by
  `packages/ui/tests/ssr-recipe-safety.test.ts`.
-->

@state {
  if (typeof HTMLElement !== 'undefined' && typeof customElements !== 'undefined') {
    class ProbeRecipeElement extends HTMLElement {
      static sheet = new CSSStyleSheet()

      connectedCallback() {
        if (!this.shadowRoot) this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' })
        this.shadowRoot.adoptedStyleSheets = [ProbeRecipeElement.sheet]
      }
    }

    if (!customElements.get('probe-recipe')) {
      customElements.define('probe-recipe', ProbeRecipeElement)
    }
  }
}

@template {
  <span>RECIPE-OK</span>
}
